Oz: Unlagged 2.01's lag compensation (Neil "haste" Toronto, GPL v2 or later: www.ra.is/unlagged), fitted to
Oz's game. The server traces an instant hit (machine gun, shotgun, lightning gun, railgun, and in Oz the
gauntlet) against every other player where the shooter saw him, at the shooter's command time, from a
history of each player's place kept by time (g_unlagged.c), never further back than g_delagMax ms; a player
whose commands miss server frames is moved on along his path (skip correction). The shooter's cgame draws his
own rail, shotgun and machine gun shots as he fires them, from the same seed the server takes, and drops the
server's events for them (cg_unlagged.c). g_delagHitscan 0 is id's game exactly; cg_delag and cg_cmdTimeNudge
are each player's, cg_projectileNudge draws the others' missiles ahead. Left out: Unlagged's missile pass (it
moved no one), its lag simulation, true ping, optimized prediction and the lightning gun (game patch 0023).

